IMPORT prelude

-- Stamp Duty Act 1978 (NT) and Taxation Administration Act 2007 (NT) -- shared nouns for the seat-neutral core.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. This is not an official version of either Act. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by
-- the Northern Territory; the statutory words quoted in these modules are reproduced from the unofficial copies at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ (Stamp Duty Act reprint REPS013, as in force 1 July 2025) and
-- ../../../taxation-administration-act-2007/registers/source-bundle/ (TAA reprint REPT039, as in force 1 July 2024),
-- under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 Oct 2026 (see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md). For the authoritative text see legislation.nt.gov.au.
--
-- TAA s 5(3): "Each taxation law (apart from this Act) must be read together with this Act as a single Act." TAA
-- s 3A(1)(c) makes the Stamp Duty Act a taxation law. So the parties and acts of both Acts are declared once here, and
-- one regulative rule may combine a duty under one Act with a step under the other (s 128 of the TAA does).
--
-- This module holds: arithmetic and date helpers, the explicit "not covered" answers, and the parties and acts of the
-- regulative rules. It states no rule of either Act.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Shared nouns -- Stamp Duty Act 1978 and Taxation Administration Act 2007 (NT)`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- Schedule 1 cl 5(2) charges "$3 for every $100 or fractional part of $100": a part of $100 counts as a whole $100.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of 100-dollar parts in` MEANS
    IF `amount` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES 100 EQUALS `amount`
         THEN `amount` DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 1

§§ `Dates`

-- Dates are DATE values. The prelude has no ordering on DATE, so days are compared by their serial numbers.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD `y` `m` `d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `first` IS A DATE, `last` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day falls from` `the day` `to` `first` `and` `last` IF
        DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `first`
    AND DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `last`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is before` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is on or after` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is on or before` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `other`

-- "n years after" a day: the same day and month n years later. READING: 29 February is taken to 28 February in a
-- year that has no 29 February (the Acts do not say). "12 months after" a day is taken as 1 year after it.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `n`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `n`)

§§ `Answers outside the deposited text`

-- Where a question reaches a figure or a period that the deposited reprints do not contain, the answer says so.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`
    `the conveyance was first executed before 4 May 2010; the home concessions as they stood before the 2010 amendments (s 102) are not in the deposited reprint`

DECLARE `Duty answer` IS ONE OF
    `the duty, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the parties and the acts`

-- The parties the two Acts name. The Commissioner of Territory Revenue, the Registrar of motor vehicles and NTCAT are
-- parties to rules, never seats.
DECLARE `Duty party` IS ONE OF
    `the conveyee`
    `the applicant for registration`
    `the transferor of the vehicle`
    `the Commissioner`
    `the Registrar`
    `the taxpayer`
    `the person affected by the decision`
    `the decision maker`

DECLARE `Objection outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the objection is allowed in full`
    `the objection is allowed in part only`
    `the objection is disallowed`

DECLARE `Duty act` IS ONE OF
    `lodge the instrument with the Commissioner for assessment`
    `pay the duty`
    `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure to occupy`
    `reassess duty on the conveyance without the concession`
    `reassess duty on the conveyance with the concession`
    `refund the duty paid`
    `pay the Registrar the duty on the certificate`
    `notify the amount received as consideration for the transfer`
    `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail`
    `give written notice of the decision on the objection` HAS `outcome` IS AN `Objection outcome`
    `apply to NTCAT for review of the decision on the objection`
    `appeal to the Supreme Court against the decision on the objection`
    `pay the penalty tax`
